issue.description:
Apply a small typography correction to the Design system → Colors preview.

## Context

<issue id="7d6f37e2-3db4-4a1f-a06e-a980b219a0eb" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-126/refine-design-system-group-and-token-label-hierarchy">PUI-126</issue> intentionally strengthened the semantic color group headings such as PRIMARY, SECONDARY, ACCENT, BASE, CARD, POPOVER, MUTED, DESTRUCTIVE, BORDER / INPUT / RING, CHARTS, and SIDEBAR.

The uppercase treatment and hierarchy are correct, but the current heading size is visually too large.

## Change

Reduce only the semantic color group heading font size back to:

`text-sm`

## Preserve

Keep everything else from the accepted <issue id="7d6f37e2-3db4-4a1f-a06e-a980b219a0eb" href="https://linear.app/emman-systems/issue/PUI-126/refine-design-system-group-and-token-label-hierarchy">PUI-126</issue> hierarchy unchanged:

* group headings remain uppercase;
* group headings continue using the base foreground semantic color;
* token labels remain normal title case;
* token labels retain their current smaller supporting size;
* HEX values remain unchanged and visually secondary;
* swatch dimensions remain unchanged;
* token grouping/order remains unchanged;
* two-column layout remains unchanged;
* current spacing and section structure remain unchanged unless a tiny adjustment is strictly required by the size change.

## Do not change

Do not modify:

* section heading sizes such as Colors / Type scale;
* token display-label wording;
* Sidebar display-label mapping;
* actual token keys;
* CSS variables;
* Theme v3;
* aliases;
* import/export;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry;
* dependencies or network behavior.

## Acceptance

* Semantic color group headings render at `text-sm`.
* Group headings remain uppercase.
* Group headings continue using base foreground.
* Token labels remain title case and unchanged in size.
* HEX values remain unchanged.
* Swatches, layout, mappings, Theme v3, persistence, Design Command, mutation boundaries, and registry remain unchanged.
